"""Frozen standalone prompt used by the accepted four-camera samples."""

PROMPT_VERSION = "whitebox_four_camera_v1"

def generation_prompt(appearance):
    return "TASK: Generate a photorealistic, synchronized four-camera driving video from these semantic whitebox videos.\nINPUTS: CAM_F0.mp4 = front; CAM_L0.mp4 = left; CAM_R0.mp4 = right; CAM_B0.mp4 = rear. Each input is 7 seconds,10 frames per second,70 frames,640x360. They share the same world and timestamps. Preserve each view's perspective, field of view and image-space camera motion. Do not swap, mirror or rotate the views.\nGEOMETRY AND MOTION: Follow the projected object boxes, silhouettes, headings, scales and temporal motion in each whitebox frame. Maintain consistent identities and appearance between views and across time. Do not add, remove, duplicate, teleport, reverse or reroute visible traffic actors. Do not invent a maneuver from the environment description. The source represents approximately2Hz log annotations interpolated to10Hz, not10Hz sensor ground truth. Cuboid occlusion and planar roads are approximate; unseen surfaces and missing annotations remain uncertain.\nSEMANTIC COLORS: #4785E8 blue=vehicle; #F073AE pink=pedestrian; #43C6B5 teal=bicycle coarse source class; #F29B38 orange=traffic cone; #9C73D8 purple=barrier; #F2D45A yellow=construction sign; #A2ADB8 gray=generic or unknown object. These colors are class codes, NOT physical paint. No individual actor's real paint, make or subtype is provided. Do not make every blue box the same blue car. The coarse bicycle label does not establish a pedal-cycle versus motorcycle subtype. Any chosen appearance must remain consistent over all four views and time; it is not a verified restoration. Colors may vary slightly after video compression. GROUND COLORS: dark slate #374355=lane surface; #293440=drivable area; #303d4b=intersection; #334344=parking area; dark green #295346=walkway, NOT necessarily grass; purple #6b5784=crosswalk, NOT purple pavement; #738190=map boundary; pale gray #bdc9d7=other selected map surface; pale blue-gray #dbe4ee=unmodeled background. Road bands and polygon edges are map proxies, not proof of exact lane-paint location. Unmodeled background does not establish the real sky color or weather.\nSCENE APPEARANCE: " + appearance + '\nUse this prose for material, environment and illumination only. Avoid placing every listed landmark in every camera. Keep static structures static, lighting coherent and textures stable. Do not reconstruct signage text, plates or logos. Only these four videos and this text are supplied; no JSON, depth maps, per-object appearance matches or reference photographs are required or assumed.\nNEGATIVE PROMPT: identity swaps, inconsistent camera appearance, invented actors, wrong class, duplicated landmarks, geometry drift, box-to-road misalignment, reversed time, abrupt texture changes, flicker, warping, hallucinated text, uniform semantic-color paint.\n'
